<template><div><p>Admin can import products added on his Shopify Store to <a href="http://localhost:8080/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Multivendor Marketplace for Shopify</a>, after this, the admin needs to assign those products to the sellers.</p>
<p>Now, to make the products appear in the Product menu, you need to assign the imported products to the sellers. Then only, the orders will be created in the Multi-vendor App.</p>
<h2 id="let-s-see-how-the-admin-can-do-this" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#let-s-see-how-the-admin-can-do-this"><span>Let's see how the Admin can do this:</span></a></h2>
<p>Go to: Multivendor Marketplace Admin Panel &gt; Products &gt; Import Products &gt; Click on the 'Import Products' button:</p>
<p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/Import-Product-From-Shopify-Admin.png" alt="Import Product From Shopify Admin"></p>
<p>On the redirected page, the admin will get two different methods to import the products in bulk:</p>
<p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/Import-Product-From-Shopify-Admin-1.png" alt="Import Product From Shopify Admin (1)"></p>
<p><strong>Method 1:</strong></p>
<p>Import products by date range; select the FROM &amp; TO dates between which you want the products from your Shopify store to get imported in your Multivendor Marketplace.</p>
<p>Note: You need to choose the date range accordingly while importing products because only those products will be imported which are available under the date range selected by you.</p>
<p><strong>Method 2:</strong></p>
<p>Import products via CSV file; the admin can also download a dummy CSV file for reference.</p>
<h2 id="assign-imported-products-to-sellers" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#assign-imported-products-to-sellers"><span>Assign Imported Products to Sellers</span></a></h2>
<p>The imported products will be listed on the following page-</p>
<p>Multivendor Marketplace Admin Panel &gt; Products &gt; Import Products:</p>
<p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/Import-Product-From-Shopify-Admin-2.png" alt="Import Product From Shopify Admin (2)"></p>
<p>Now, the admin needs to click on the three dots (<strong>⋅⋅⋅</strong>) under the ACTION menu &amp; then click on the 'Assign product to seller' button. This action will give you a pop-up:</p>
<p><img src="https://cdnblog.webkul.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/Import-Product-From-Shopify-Admin-3.png" alt="Import Product From Shopify Admin (3)"></p>
<p>On this pop-up, the admin can change the product type (normal/global/digital) &amp; then he needs to enter the seller email ID.</p>
<p><strong>Mark</strong>:<br>
If the product has variants then admin can't change the product type to Global/Digital while assigning them to the seller.</p>
<h3 id="demo-details" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#demo-details"><span>Demo Details</span></a></h3>
<p>Check out: <a href="https://multivendor-marketplace-5.myshopify.com/pages/seller-profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://multivendor-marketplace-5.myshopify.com/pages/demo</a></p>
</div></template>


